        // The actual sender in newEmergencyOracle is the test contract, but within the VM prank, msg.sender is the test contract.
        // The nonce of the test contract at the time of the call will be the nonce after setUp (which deployed nothing else).
        // Since setUp only deploys C, which has a different address, the test contract's nonce is still 1 before the call.
        // Thus, the deployed EmergencyOracle address is predictable.

