        // The nonce before the call is the current nonce of the contract before the transaction. Since we are inside a test function,
        // the nonce of this contract may be >0. We need to compute the address using the nonce at the time of the call.
        // We can capture the event data by using a fallback receiver? No.
        // The instructions allow reading c's public surface, but the new oracle is not stored in C. We cannot directly get its address.
        // However, we can observe the difference by checking the owner of the new oracle. But we need the address.
