        Vm.Log[] memory logs = vm.getRecordedLogs();
        // The first log should be the NewEmergencyOracle event. The event signature is keccak256("NewEmergencyOracle(address,address)")
        // The indexed parameters are not indexed? The event is:
        // event NewEmergencyOracle(address owner, address newOracle);
        // Since no indexed keyword, both are in the data. So the topic0 is the event signature, topic1... not used, data contains the two addresses.
        // So the data is abi.encode(owner, newOracle). We can decode it.
        require(logs.length >= 1, "No logs");
        (address owner, address newOracle) = abi.decode(logs[0].data, (address, address));

        // Now we can read the owner of the new oracle via its public owner() getter.
        // The EmergencyOracle has a public owner() view returns (address). We can call it with the address.
        // We need to interact with the new oracle through its public interface, but we don't have its ABI in this test.
